<programme start="20261012040000 +0000" stop="20261012070000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">LSU at Kentucky</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 10 Tigers face the Wildcats at Kroger Field. LSU has won two straight, beating the Cowboys 63-14 behind Sam Leavitt&apos;s three TDs. Kentucky is on a three-game win streak, edging South Carolina 35-34 in OT behind three Kenny Minchey TDs.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261012070000 +0000" stop="20261012100000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Florida at Missouri</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 8 Florida Gators battle the No. 25 Missouri Tigers at Memorial Stadium in a Week 5 SEC showdown. Florida enters this game with a perfect 4-0 record, while Missouri (3-1) dropped its first game by losing to Mississippi State, 31-24, last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261012100000 +0000" stop="20261012140000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">Unsportsmanlike with Evan, Canty and Michelle</title><desc lang="en">Start the day off right with Chris Canty, Evan Cohen and Michelle Smallmon providing an energizing and informative way to take on the day. Sports, life and laughter are what it&apos;s all about.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Talk Show</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25542634_b_v8_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261012140000 +0000" stop="20261012170000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Kansas at Utah</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Kansas Jayhawks (2-2) play the No. 12 Utah Utes (4-0) at Rice-Eccles Stadium. Utah is unbeaten in four games, beating Iowa State 31-17 behind Devon Dampier&apos;s two TDs. Kansas shut out Middle Tennessee 55-0 behind Dylan Edwards&apos; three TDs.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261012170000 +0000" stop="20261012200000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Georgia at Alabama</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 2 Georgia Bulldogs (5-0) face the No. 6 Alabama Crimson Tide (5-0) at Bryant-Denny Stadium. Both franchises are unbeaten in five games, with Georgia beating Vanderbilt 38-14 and Alabama beating No. 17 Mississippi State 56-23.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ab.jpg"/></programme>
