<programme start="20261011110000 +0000" stop="20261011130000 +0000" channel="NBC Sports Network"><title lang="en">Premier League Soccer</title><sub-title lang="en">Sunderland vs. Brighton &amp; Hove Albion</sub-title><desc lang="en">Sunderland (1-1-3) hosts Brighton &amp; Hove Albion (3-1-1) at the Stadium of Light. Brighton arrives unbeaten in three games and off a 3-0 win over Arsenal. Sunderland, 14th after conceding five to Manchester City, is winless in two against Brighton.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Soccer</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p3605402_b_v12_bj.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261011130000 +0000" stop="20261011150000 +0000" channel="NBC Sports Network"><title lang="en">Premier League Soccer</title><sub-title lang="en">Hull City vs. Everton</sub-title><desc lang="en">Hull City (2-2-1) hosts Everton (2-3-0) at MKM Stadium in Premier League Matchweek 6. Eighth-place Hull lost to Newcastle in Matchweek 5, while seventh-place Everton beat Crystal Palace 2-0 behind goals from Kiernan Dewsbury-Hall and Barry.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Soccer</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p3605402_b_v12_bj.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261011150000 +0000" stop="20261011170000 +0000" channel="NBC Sports Network"><title lang="en">Premier League Soccer</title><sub-title lang="en">Manchester United vs. Tottenham Hotspur</sub-title><desc lang="en">Manchester United (1-2-2) hosts Tottenham Hotspur (0-2-3) at Old Trafford in the Premier League. The Red Devils arrive 12th after a 1-1 draw with the Cottagers, while 20th-place Spurs arrive having fallen 3-0 to the Bees in their previous match.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Soccer</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p3605402_b_v12_bj.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261011170000 +0000" stop="20261011190000 +0000" channel="NBC Sports Network"><title lang="en">Premier League Soccer</title><sub-title lang="en">Chelsea vs. Bournemouth</sub-title><desc lang="en">Chelsea (2-1-2) hosts Bournemouth (0-3-2) at Stamford Bridge in the Premier League. Chelsea arrives 10th after five games following a 3-0 loss at Brentford. Bournemouth, 17th, has drawn three of five meetings here - including a 2-2 draw in December.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Soccer</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p3605402_b_v12_bj.jpg"/></programme>
